post in a separate exec after an edit. Comments are not part of the edit's undo step.","category":"helpers","examples":["helpers.addComment('Should this arrow be dashed?', { shapeId: 'box1' })","helpers.addComment('Room for a legend here', { x: 400, y: 120 })","helpers.addComment('Done: both boxes widened.', { threadId: 'comment-thread:abc' })"]},{"name":"createMermaidDiagram","kind":"method","signature":"createMermaidDiagram(source: string, options?: { mermaidConfig?: Record<string, any>; blueprintRender?: { position?: { x: number; y: number }; centerOnPosition?: boolean } }): Promise<{ rootShapeId: TLShapeId; shapeIds: TLShapeId[]; bounds: { x: number; y: number; w: number; h: number } }>","description":"Draw a mermaid diagram as real, editable tldraw shapes: geo shapes and bound arrows, grouped under rootShapeId (when the diagram has only one top-level shape, such as a lone node or a subgraph holding the rest, rootShapeId is that shape). A subgraph or compound state is a rectangle geo shape whose children are its nodes and whose richText is its title. Await it. Supports flowchart/graph, sequenceDiagram, stateDiagram-v2 and mindmap; any other kind throws, so build those from shapes. Centred on the viewport by default; blueprintRender.position is a page point the diagram is centred on, or its top-left corner when centerOnPosition is false. mermaidConfig passes through to mermaid (e.g. { flowchart: { curve: 'linear' } }). A diagram placed wholly inside a frame goes into it; one straddling a frame's edge can be clipped by the frame or left beside it. A ```mermaid fence around the source is fine. Throws mermaid's parse error for invalid source, having drawn nothing. Returns every created shape id and the diagram's page bounds, so a second diagram can be placed beside the first.","category":"helpers","examples":["await helpers.createMermaidDiagram('flowchart TD\n  A[Start] --> B{Ship it?}\n  B -->|Yes| C[Release]\n  B -->|No| D[Fix]')","const first = await helpers.createMermaidDiagram(a)
